---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Why would I pick PNG over JPG for a page?',
    a: 'PNG writes every pixel exactly, so text edges and line drawings stay perfectly sharp, and nothing is lost if the picture is edited and saved again. The price is weight: a PNG of a page runs larger than a JPG of the same page. On our five-page test document at screen size, the PNG set came out at 153 KB against the JPG set\'s 80.3 KB, about twice the weight; on a photograph page the gap grows. For photos and quick sharing, the PDF to JPG page is the lighter road.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I turn the pictures back into a document with selectable words?',
    a: 'No. Once a page is a picture, its words are part of the picture, the way words in a photograph are: they can be read by eye, not selected, copied or searched as text. If you need the words themselves as text, the PDF to text tool pulls out the words the file already stores, and the read a scan (OCR) tool reads words from pictures of pages.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which size should I pick?',
    a: 'Screen size (96 DPI) is right for screens, forms and sharing: a Letter page comes out 816 x 1056 pixels. Print size (200 DPI) is the sharper picture, right for printing: a Letter page comes out 1700 x 2200 pixels, and a PNG at that size is a heavy file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get the pictures?',
    a: 'A one-page PDF comes back as the PNG itself. A longer document comes back as one ZIP holding one PNG per page, named in page order, so the set stays together and stays sorted.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and its pages are drawn as pictures in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to turn PDF pages into PNG pictures",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. The page reads its page count before anything runs." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Pick the picture size", text: "Choose screen size (96 DPI) for screens and sharing, or print size (200 DPI) for printing. The format is PNG: exact, and heavier than JPG." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Turn the pages into PNG pictures", text: "Press 'Turn the pages into PNG pictures'. Every page is drawn as a PNG picture, one at a time, in your browser." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the pictures", text: "Take the finished pictures away: the PNG itself for a one-page file, or one ZIP holding every page in order." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="PDF to PNG: turn every page into a PNG picture, free · Benchzy" description="Turn every page of a PDF into an exact PNG picture, at screen or print size, inside your browser. One PNG per page, named in order; nothing is uploaded.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · convert</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">PDF to PNG</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Turn every page of a PDF into a PNG picture: exact pixels, at screen size or print
        size. Everything runs in your browser; the document is never uploaded. The honest
        trade, stated first: PNG files run larger than JPG, often much larger. If the
        lighter file serves you better, the same pages as JPG are on the
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/pdf-to-jpg/">PDF to JPG page</a>.
        And one warning that cannot be undone: once a page is a picture, its words are
        part of the picture and cannot be selected or searched as text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="pj-tool" data-preset-key="pdf-to-png" data-tool-name="PDF to PNG">
      <div id="pj-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="pj-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="pj-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Picture kind</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pj-format" value="png" checked disabled />
              <span>PNG, exact (this door's format: nothing thrown away, and the heavier file)</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Picture size</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pj-dpi" value="96" checked />
              <span>Screen size, 96 DPI (a Letter page becomes 816 x 1056 pixels)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pj-dpi" value="200" />
              <span>Print size, 200 DPI (a Letter page becomes 1700 x 2200 pixels)</span>
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="pj-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            Before you run it: the words on each page become part of its picture. They can
            still be read by eye, but they cannot be selected, copied or searched as text
            afterwards.
          </p>
          <button id="pj-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Turn the pages into PNG pictures</button>
          <p id="pj-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="pj-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="pj-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="pj-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="pj-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the pictures</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For pages that must stay pixel-exact: diagrams, forms to edit in a picture program, pages headed for print or for another tool that wants PNG." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PDF' }, { n: '02', t: 'Pick the picture size' }, { n: '03', t: 'Turn the pages into PNG pictures and download' }]} />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Each page is drawn onto a fresh sheet at the size you picked, the way a reader
          shows it, and saved as a PNG exactly: no quality setting, nothing thrown away.
          Pages are drawn one at a time and packed as they finish, into the PNG itself for
          a one-page file or one ZIP for a longer one, with the pictures named in page
          order. The download is how we protect your privacy: the program that does this
          job is part of this page, loaded from this site, and your file is read into the
          page and never uploaded.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          PNG is the heavy format: in our test on a five-page document at screen size, the
          PNG pictures together weighed 153 KB against the same pages' 80.3 KB as JPG. The
          pictures are also held in your device's memory until they are packed, so the
          limit on a long document is the device itself: in our tests a 50-page document
          rendered page by page at screen size without trouble, and print size makes each
          picture roughly four times the memory. Pages are drawn over white, the way they
          look on paper, so a page drawn with see-through parts does not come out
          see-through.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF cannot be opened by this tool. Take its password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/pdf-to-jpg.js';
  </script>
</Base>
